From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:58:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(usage): show the current decode speed beside the run
 average
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The run indicator carried a single reading — the run-wide average — which creeps
upward as more calls finish. Adds the "current" number next to it: the decode
speed of the run's most recently finished call, so the value holds still while a
long tool runs instead of drifting.

- server: `foldDecodeCallResult` also remembers the last call's span and tokens
  and `latestRunSpeed` exposes them; `usage.updated` now carries `speedLatest`
  beside the existing `speed` (the run-wide average), and both are reset when a
  new run takes over the fold state.
- client store: keeps a `runSpeedLatest` map beside `runSpeed`, filled from the
  same event so neither can tick between events, and clears both together.
- chat view: the run indicator renders 当前 + 平均 side by side; the settled
  average still lands on the turn's message when the run ends.

`chat.tokensPerSecond` splits into `chat.tokensPerSecondCurrent` /
`chat.tokensPerSecondAverage` across all 11 locales.
